('CIT_ISL_AHL_BAYT_QUR','ENT_ISL_AHL_BAYT','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 33:33','And stay in your houses. Bedizen not yourselves with the bedizenment of the Time of Ignorance. Be regular in prayer, and pay the poor-due, and obey Allah and His messenger. Allah''s wish is but to remove uncleanness far from you, O Folk of the Household, and cleanse you with a thorough cleansing.','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#33:33','https://quran.com/33/33','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',false,NULL,DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_AL_YASA_QUR','ENT_ISL_AL_YASA','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 6:86','And Ishmael and Elisha and Jonah and Lot. Each one (of them) did We prefer above (Our) creatures,','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#6:86','https://quran.com/6/86','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_AYYUB_QUR','ENT_ISL_AYYUB','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 4:163','Lo! We inspire thee as We inspired Noah and the prophets after him, as We inspired Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac and Jacob and the tribes, and Jesus and Job and Jonah and Aaron and Solomon, and as We imparted unto David the Psalms;','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#4:163','https://quran.com/4/163','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_DAWUD_QUR','ENT_ISL_DAWUD','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 2:251','So they routed them by Allah''s leave and David slew Goliath; and Allah gave him the kingdom and wisdom, and taught him of that which He willeth. And if Allah had not repelled some men by others the earth would have been corrupted. But Allah is a Lord of Kindness to (His) creatures.','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#2:251','https://quran.com/2/251','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_DHUL_KIFL_QUR','ENT_ISL_DHUL_KIFL','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 21:85','And (mention) Ishmael, and Idris, and Dhu''l-Kifl. All were of the steadfast.','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#21:85','https://quran.com/21/85','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_ISMAIL_QUR','ENT_ISL_ISMAIL','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 2:125','And when We made the House (at Makka) a resort for mankind and sanctuary, (saying): Take as your place of worship the place where Abraham stood (to pray). And We imposed a duty upon Abraham and Ishmael, (saying): Purify My house for those who go around and those who meditate therein and those who bow down and prostrate themselves (in worship).','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#2:125','https://quran.com/2/125','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_HAMALAT_ARSH_QUR','ENT_ISL_HAMALAT_ARSH','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 40:7','Those who bear the Throne, and all who are round about it, hymn the praises of their Lord and believe in Him and ask forgiveness for those who believe (saying): Our Lord! Thou comprehendest all things in mercy and knowledge, therefor forgive those who repent and follow Thy way. Ward off from them the punishment of hell.','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#40:7','https://quran.com/40/7','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',false,NULL,DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
('CIT_ISL_HUD_QUR','ENT_ISL_HUD','SRC_QURAN','The Qur’an','Surah 7:65','And unto (the tribe of) A''ad (We sent) their brother, Hud. He said: O my people! Serve Allah. Ye have no other Allah save Him. Will ye not ward off (evil)?','Marmaduke Pickthall',1930,'https://tanzil.net/#7:65','https://quran.com/7/65','primary-verbatim','English (Pickthall); sura:ayah is translation-independent — consult the Arabic (linked).',true,'Verse located by name (no ayah in attestation); confirm it is the intended reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','deterministic sura:ayah lookup, or name-anchored where no ayah given (Pickthall, Tanzil)',1),
